If this line represents a road and the point $(2,3,4)$ represents a person standing at home at midnight, then what the question is asking is, what is the closest point on the road to the person's location?  If $\mathbf{p}$ labels the initial point of the road, then $\mathbf{p} + t \mathbf{d}$ labels the position of the person as they travel along the road, or it would be best to label this by some other vector $\mathbf{q}$.  Then, what we are asked to find is the value of $t$ so that $\mathbf{q}$ and $(2,3,4)$ have a minimum distance.

The formula $\mathbf{p} + t \mathbf{d}$ for the road is analogous to parametric equations, \[\begin{aligned} x + p &= dx \cos \theta \\ y + q &= dy \sin \theta \end{aligned}\]that defines a line.  Thus, we are trying to find the value of $t$ so that the minimum distance between $t\mathbf{d} + \mathbf{p}$ and $ (2,3,4)$.

